# Docker build context (repo root) exclusions.
#
# Every build uses the repo root as its context (server/Dockerfile copies
# `server/`, web/Dockerfile copies `web/`, transcoding/Dockerfile.agent copies
# `transcoding/`), so the per-package *.dockerignore files are inert — this file
# is the only one that applies.
#
# Secret files MUST be listed with a `**/` prefix as well as bare: a bare
# `.dev.vars` matches only a file at the context root, not `server/.dev.vars`.
.git
**/node_modules
node_modules
.pnpm-store
.pnpm-cache
**/dist
**/dist-node
**/.next
**/out
**/.wrangler
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
*.log

# Environment & secrets — never in an image. `.env` is the deployment config for
# docker compose and holds every secret the stack uses.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
**/.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars.*
secrets.json
**/secrets.json

# Context-only files the images never need.
docs
media
.dockerignore
